WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Easter, 1967. Seventeen people lost their lives
in the Norwegian mountains.

00:00:06.556 --> 00:00:11.778
The same year, the Trekking Association and the Red Cross
sent out a message that still stands:

00:00:12.222 --> 00:00:16.000
welcome to the mountains,
but take responsibility yourself.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:20.033
Nine rules. Three before you leave.

00:00:20.589 --> 00:00:23.033
Plan your trip, and tell someone where you are going.

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:26.256
Adapt the trip to your ability and the conditions.

00:00:26.589 --> 00:00:29.367
Pay attention to the weather and avalanche forecasts.

00:00:30.289 --> 00:00:31.178
Two for the pack.

00:00:31.511 --> 00:00:34.733
Be prepared for bad weather and cold,
even on short trips.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Bring what you need to help yourself and others.

00:00:38.878 --> 00:00:40.100
And four for the trail.

00:00:40.211 --> 00:00:41.322
Choose safe routes.

00:00:41.878 --> 00:00:44.767
Use a map and compass,
and always know where you are.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:48.100
Turn back in time.
There is no shame in turning around.

00:00:48.544 --> 00:00:51.211
Save your energy,
and seek shelter if necessary.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:56.800
Nine short sentences. Read them at home,
so you remember them in the storm.

